# Senj municipal cemetery, photographed 9 October 2024.
#
# 105 photographs, read out 15 September 2026. GPS on the files puts them in a
# 400 m box centred on 44.985 N, 14.924 E, all taken between 02:37 and 04:22 UTC
# on 9 October 2024 -- the Senj town cemetery, the day after the Otocac
# churchyard in sources/graves/otocac-2024-10-08.psv. The two are one trip and
# only the Otocac half had been recorded.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN THE OTOCAC SET. Five DIRECT ANCESTORS are on these
# stones: ahnentafel 2 and 3 in one tomb, ahnentafel 5 on the next stone, and
# ahnentafel 6 and 7 on a stone cross further up the hill. Three brothers of
# ahnentafel 6 are here too. Before today graves.json held 72 memorials, all of
# them Find a Grave transcriptions from Australia and Canada, and NOT ONE
# Croatian cemetery.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. A gravestone is a memorial, not a register. It is carved by the
# living, often years after the death. Two of the five ancestor stones here give
# a birth year ONE OUT from the register -- Ljubomir 1891 for 1892, Antonija 1860
# for 1859 -- while every death year on them is right. Nothing here is joined to
# the tree on the strength of the stone alone.
#
# "conf" is how the reading was made:
#   r = read at FULL RESOLUTION, cropped and enlarged 3-8x
#   p = read at reduced scale from a contact sheet; the name is secure but the
#       DIGITS ARE NOT VERIFIED and want a full-resolution pass
#   ? = uncertain, not to be relied on
#
# surname|given|born|died|stone|conf|photo
#
# --- THE DIRECT LINE ---
